# Government Schemes of India: Launch Year, Ministry, Purpose

> Almost every general-awareness paper carries two or three scheme questions: which scheme did what, in which year,
> under which ministry. The same dozen flagship schemes return again and again. This lesson groups them by purpose
> so that the launch year and the headline benefit stick together.

## 1. How Schemes Are Classified

A **Centrally Sponsored Scheme** is funded jointly by the Centre and the states. A **Central Sector Scheme** is funded wholly by the Union government. Exams rarely ask the funding pattern, but they do ask the **launch year**, the **ministry** and the **target group**.

[definition]
A **flagship scheme** is a large, high-visibility programme announced or launched at the national level, usually with a single headline benefit (a bank account, a cooking gas connection, a health cover, a cash transfer).
[/definition]

## 2. Financial Inclusion and Entrepreneurship

| Scheme | Launched | Ministry | Headline point |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana | 28 August 2014 (announced 15 August) | Finance | Basic bank account for every household, with a RuPay debit card |
| Pradhan Mantri Mudra Yojana | 8 April 2015 | Finance | Collateral-free loans to small and micro enterprises |
| PM Suraksha Bima Yojana and PM Jeevan Jyoti Bima Yojana | 9 May 2015 | Finance | Low-cost accident and life insurance |
| Atal Pension Yojana | 9 May 2015 | Finance | Pension for workers in the unorganised sector |
| Sukanya Samriddhi Yojana | January 2015 | Finance | Small-savings account for the girl child |
| Stand-Up India | April 2016 | Finance | Loans for SC, ST and women entrepreneurs |
| PM SVANidhi | June 2020 | Housing and Urban Affairs | Working-capital loans for street vendors |

Memory trick: the **three insurance and pension schemes of 2015** were announced together in May 2015, and the Jan Dhan account is their base.

## 3. Social Welfare, Health and Housing

| Scheme | Launched | Ministry | Headline point |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Beti Bachao Beti Padhao | 22 January 2015, Panipat (Haryana) | Women and Child Development, with Health and Education | Improve the child sex ratio and promote girls' education |
| Pradhan Mantri Ujjwala Yojana | 1 May 2016, Ballia (Uttar Pradesh) | Petroleum and Natural Gas | LPG connections for women from poor households |
| Ayushman Bharat PM-JAY | 23 September 2018, Ranchi | Health and Family Welfare | Health cover of Rs 5 lakh per family per year at empanelled hospitals |
| Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Urban) | June 2015 | Housing and Urban Affairs | Housing for urban poor |
| Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Gramin) | 2016 | Rural Development | Housing for rural poor |
| Poshan Abhiyaan | March 2018 | Women and Child Development | Fight malnutrition among children, adolescent girls and mothers |
| National Food Security Act | 2013 | Consumer Affairs, Food and Public Distribution | Legal right to subsidised food grains |

Haryana students should remember that **Beti Bachao Beti Padhao was launched at Panipat**, a very frequent state-paper question.

## 4. Rural Development, Agriculture and Water

| Scheme | Launched | Ministry | Headline point |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| MGNREGA | 2005 (as NREGA) | Rural Development | Legal guarantee of up to 100 days of wage work per rural household |
| PM-KISAN | February 2019 | Agriculture and Farmers Welfare | Rs 6,000 a year to farmer families in three instalments |
| Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana | 2016 | Agriculture and Farmers Welfare | Crop insurance |
| Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana | 2000 | Rural Development | All-weather rural road connectivity |
| Jal Jeevan Mission | August 2019 | Jal Shakti | Tap water connection for rural households; 55 litres per person per day |
| Swachh Bharat Mission | 2 October 2014 | Jal Shakti (rural) and Housing and Urban Affairs (urban) | Sanitation and elimination of open defecation |

The MGNREGA law dates from 2005. In December 2025, Parliament passed a new rural employment law intended to replace it, so confirm the latest position in current-affairs sources. Questions on the 2005 Act still stay valid as historical facts.

## 5. Industry, Skills, Technology and Energy

| Scheme | Launched | Ministry | Headline point |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Make in India | 25 September 2014 | Commerce and Industry (DPIIT) | Promote manufacturing in India |
| Digital India | 1 July 2015 | Electronics and IT | Digitally empower the country |
| Skill India | 15 July 2015 | Skill Development and Entrepreneurship | Train youth for jobs |
| Smart Cities Mission | June 2015 | Housing and Urban Affairs | Modernise selected cities |
| AMRUT | June 2015 | Housing and Urban Affairs | Water supply and sewerage in cities |
| PM Vishwakarma | 17 September 2023 | Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises | Support for traditional artisans |
| PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana | February 2024 | New and Renewable Energy | Rooftop solar systems for households |

## 6. Older Landmark Schemes

| Scheme | Launched | Headline point |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Integrated Child Development Services (ICDS) | 2 October 1975 | Nutrition, health and pre-school education for young children and mothers |
| Mid-Day Meal Scheme | 15 August 1995 (nationwide) | Cooked meal for school children; now called PM POSHAN |
| Antyodaya Anna Yojana | 2000 | Subsidised grain for the poorest households |
| Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan | 2001 | Universal elementary education |
| National Rural Health Mission | 2005 | Strengthen rural health care |

Older schemes are asked less often but appear in SSC and state papers as "which scheme began in 1975?" style questions.

## 7. Common Traps and Quick Ways to Remember

- **2014**: Jan Dhan, Swachh Bharat, Make in India. **2015**: Digital India, Skill India, Mudra, the insurance trio, BBBP and Smart Cities. **2016**: Ujjwala, Stand-Up India.
- Ujjwala and PM-JAY both start with a "target group" (women from poor homes, poor families); do not swap their ministries (Petroleum vs Health).
- Swachh Bharat has two ministries: Jal Shakti for rural and Housing and Urban Affairs for urban.
- PM-KISAN pays Rs 6,000 a year, not a month.
- Do not mix the Jan Dhan **announcement** (15 August) with its **launch** (28 August).

[example]
A question asks: "Beti Bachao Beti Padhao was launched from which place?" Panipat is correct. Options like Ballia (Ujjwala) and Ranchi (PM-JAY) are the scheme launch sites that get swapped. Link the three: Panipat is Haryana (BBBP, 2015), Ballia is Uttar Pradesh (Ujjwala, 2016) and Ranchi is Jharkhand (PM-JAY, 2018).
[/example]

[summary]
Schemes are best remembered by year, ministry and the main benefit. Jan Dhan (2014), Swachh Bharat (2014), Make in India (2014), Digital India, Skill India, Mudra and the insurance trio (2015), Ujjwala (2016), PM-JAY (2018), PM-KISAN (2019), Jal Jeevan Mission (2019), PM Vishwakarma (2023) and PM Surya Ghar (2024). Beti Bachao Beti Padhao began at Panipat on 22 January 2015, Ujjwala at Ballia and PM-JAY at Ranchi. PM-JAY gives Rs 5 lakh of cover and PM-KISAN pays Rs 6,000 a year. Keep the two Swachh Bharat ministries and the Jan Dhan dates apart.
[/summary]
